<title>USA: U.S. cash soymeal - Basis firms on slowing crush.</title>
<headline>U.S. cash soymeal - Basis firms on slowing crush.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Basis levels for soymeal were firm on Wednesday with supplies continuing to tighten amid signs that the crush is slowing down, cash sources said.</p>
<p>&quot;Margins have dictated that there has been some reduction (in the crush pace),&quot; one Indiana crusher source said.</p>
<p>Last week NOPA put the weekly crush at 30.06 million bushels, down from 30.48 million a week earlier. A further slowdown was expected when data is issued on Thursday.</p>
<p>Dealers also noted talk that a leading central Illinois processor had run out of supplies for January delivery and was buying from another nearby location.  </p>
